+    // ---- Suspension kits (journal v8) ----
+    // A bought GT4 kit is a contract we enforce, not a part the engine installs: the sheet takes any value and the
+    // physics consumes it (docs/E4-SUSPENSION-MECHANISM-2026-09-18.md). So the journal stores what was bought, what
+    // is fitted and what the player dialled, indexed by the SAME slot as the engine tuning records - one identity per
+    // car and colour, no second allocator. Six settings per slot: spring front/rear, ride front/rear, camber
+    // front/rear. Each is stored as value + 1, so a zero means "never set" and the kit's own default applies; every
+    // ported value is well under 255. Kits owned are a bit each, so a car keeps what it paid for after a downgrade.
+    static SUSP_VALUES = 6;
