+    // ---- Journal v10: the tuning records are sized by the journal, not by a constant ----
+    // v8 wrote 32 records by 7 part types into every save whether or not a single car had been tuned, and the 33rd
+    // paid configuration had nowhere to go ("All 32 tuning records are in use"). v9 stores the record count, the part
+    // type stride and the suspension stride in the header and sizes the arrays from them: a career that tuned two
+    // cars carries eight records, a full garage grows to as many as it paid for, and a new part type costs nothing
+    // until this build defines it. The number of records is NOT the size of the garage - a record is one car code
+    // and colour that has something paid for or dialled on it.
+    // The ceiling of paid configurations, and the bound on a garbage journal. It is set by the SAVE, not by the
+    // shop: the packed journal is a ByteData the save wrapper holds while Deflate asks for its 350 KB block, and
+    // on the release ISO (v0.21.1, journal v11, 2026-09-21, docs/evidence/p5-gates-20260921/README.md) a packed
+    // journal of 33 188 bytes (256 x 70 + 15 268) became a 64 KB block that no longer fitted under the boot-time
+    // stack, fell into the save's hole and left 301 KB of the 350 needed: every in-career save went out raw. At
+    // 32 628 bytes (248 records) it stayed a 32 KB block and the hole was 366 KB. So: base + cap x record < 32 768.
+    // The current v13 base is 12 778 (measured below): 192 x 82 + 12 778 = 28 522, 4 246 bytes under the 32 KB
+    // boundary. 240 records would leave only 310 bytes; 248 would cross it. The 192 cap also limits the popup's
+    // resident load, already tight on a full journal. Keep a multiple of RECORD_GROW so capFor cannot step past it.
+    // scripts/test_journal_cap.py holds the current serialization arithmetic offline.
+    // 25.09: the retail GT4 events add 126 events and 40 championship blocks to the base (about 6.8 KB), so the cap
+    // drops to 128 tuned cars: 20 733 + 128 x 82 = 31 229, 1 539 under the block (the 1 024 margin holds).
+    static RECORDS_MAX = 128;
+    static RECORD_GROW = 8;     // records are added a block at a time, because growing rebuilds the whole structure
+    // Frozen strides of the v9 layout. The record count varies, the two strides do not: the loader has to work out
+    // the capacity from the file size ALONE (see capOfSize), and it cannot solve one equation with three unknowns.
+    // When a later build needs more part types or suspension fields, it freezes these two and adds v10; the header
+    // carries both numbers so that reader can tell what it is looking at without guessing.
+    // Two fields per record hold the tyres: which grades this car has paid for (eleven bits, categories 100..110)
+    // and which one it wears. Tyres are not another tuning type - a grade has no stage ladder - and eleven grades
+    // do not fit the five-bit owned mask the types use, so they get their own fields.
