+    // What one record costs and what the rest of the journal costs. MEASURED IN THE GAME, never computed from a
+    // byte formula - this VM frames a structure with more than its fields, and the two-field header alone is 39
+    // bytes, not 8. The r7 fixture builds three real layouts of each version and fails if these four numbers stop
+    // describing them, exactly as it guards LAYOUT_SIZES for v1..v8.
+    //   v10 8 records = 15828, 16 = 16388, 24 = 16948  ->  70 per record, 15268 without records
+    //   v12: the record grows by six STByte elements (three stages, three owned masks). The v9 -> v10 step showed
+    //   what an element costs in this VM - one STShort and one STByte added exactly 5 bytes, payload plus one frame
+    //   byte each - so 70 + 6 x 2 = 82, and the base does not move because no array was added. EXPECTED, not yet
+    //   measured: r7 step 12 must print 8 = 15924, 16 = 16580, 24 = 17236 and fit=1 before this build is released;
+    //   if it prints other numbers, the measured ones go here and the expectation was wrong, not the fixture.
+    // They are constants and not a measurement taken at load for a reason: building and serializing four layouts on
+    // every boot left the heap in a shape where the save compressor's 350 KB block no longer fitted - measured
+    // 2026-09-20, the same scenario giving 409 KB with the constants and 341 KB with the four builds.
+    // v13: the series array shrank from EVENTS x SERIES_BLOCK to SERIES_SLOTS x SERIES_BLOCK, that is from
+    // 170 to 34 blocks. 136 blocks x 27 elements x 2 serialized bytes = 7 344 bytes less, so 15 268 - 7 344.
